  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia continues to provide advisory support to the Autonomous Bougainville Government (ABG) through the Bougainville Partnership, helping build accountability and governance. Support included: 1) assistance to the Department of Treasury and Finance to finalise a Finance Manual required under the Public Finance (Management and Administration) Act 2014. This enabled the introduction of an One Line Budget Information System (OLBIS), improving financial oversight and accountability; 2) advisory support to the Department of Justice and Legal Services to prioritise legislative reforms aligned with Bougainville&#x2019;s economic strategy, including work on the draft Bougainville Taxes Act 2025; 3) collaboration with the Office of the Chief Secretary and Department of Personnel Management and Administrative Services to deliver the fifth phase of senior recruitment, supporting transparent and merit-based selection processes; 4) advice to the Department of Primary Industries to strengthen planning and internal governance; and 5) support to the Office of the Bougainville Electoral Commissioner in the lead-up to the 2025 ABG elections, including assistance with voter roll updates and operational planning.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2021, we supported the Autonomous Bougainville Government with the recruitment process for 16 Head of Department positions. The incumbents for these positions were all appointed in an acting capacity, which limited their effectiveness and authority. By December 2022, 13 of 16 positions were filled. Support included establishing selection panels, developing screening procedures, interviewing, and selecting candidates, and preparing reports for the Bougainville Senior Appointments Committee. The Program also assisted with the drafting of a Department of Personnel Management and Administrative Services HR Manual, a Training Policy, a Procedures Manual, and a DPMAS Corporate Plan.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Disability equity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2023, under our Strongim Social Capital Modality (SSCM), we provided support to the Bougainville Disabled Persons Organisation (BDPO) for institutional capacity support. An organisational capacity assessment was conducted and one of the recommendations is to develop a capacity development plan, 6-month workplan, monitoring and evaluation framework and risk register. With the support of the PNG Assembly of Disabled Persons (PNGADP). The organisation was able to undergo training in early June to help with awareness raising of the new Bougainville Disability Policy working closely with the Department for Community Development.  Our support also helped the organisation to hold its annual general meeting and elect its new office bearers.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Our investment continues to provide advisory support to key departments in the Autonomous Bougainville Government, assisting its draw-down of powers and functions from the National government to be able to provide services and be accountable to the people of Bougainville. Legislative advisory support in 2023 included: (i) the Departments of Personnel Management and Administrative Services and Justice and Legal Services were supported to review the existing draft Public Service Bill and General Orders for Bougainville.  We supported, drafting instructions for a modern public service for Bougainville including induction manuals and job orientations; (ii) the Bougainville Land Policy was reviewed, and drafting instructions developed for four Bills for a modified land regulation regime for the region; and (iii) drafting instructions were also developed to regulate and employ teachers in Bougainville with a selective review of the Bougainville Mining Act (BMA) 2015 commenced, initiated at the direction of the Bougainville Executive Council.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender equality</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the Bougainville Women&#x2019;s Federation began in late 2023. The program aims to build on the Federation&#x2019;s established reputation as the premier women&#x2019;s peak body in Bougainville and relationships forged through its mentorship programs for young women. It has prioritised advocacy with and for Bougainvillean women through District and Regional Women&#x2019;s Associations and in collaboration with Bougainville House of Representatives (BHoR) and the regional women&#x2019;s representatives.  With Australian support, BWF has a strengthened capacity to undertake its mandated function to promote women&#x2019;s leadership in political and civil spaces in Bougainville.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The regulatory environment for Bougainville commodities is a key focus of our support under the Economic Development Pillar. In 2022 support was provided to Bougainville to collaboratively draft an Economic Sector Strategic Plan followed by a Trade and Investment Conference held in October 2022. Support to the Bougainville Government&#x2019;s (ABG) Department for Primary Industry has resulted in increased capacity within the department to address priority policies and legislation for the Agriculture, Livestock and Fisheries sectors. A Memorandum of Agreement (MoA) signed in October 2022 between the ABG, and the PNG Coconut and Cocoa Board has enhanced intergovernmental dialogue.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Infrastructure</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under our Investment, the Bougainville Partnership supported the construction of 19 Community Government Buildings, a laboratory and office at the Bougainville Agricultural Commodity Regulatory Act facility (BACRA), and extensions to the Bougainville Technical College Administration and Classroom Building. Key principles adopted in the design and construction included disability accessibility and environmental and other safeguards in line with DFAT&#x2019;s requirements and internationally agreed standards.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under our investment we provide support to the Department of Primary Industries (DPI) with the implementation of Bougainville Commodities Regulation (Amendment) Act 2022 (BCRA) and the operationalisation of Bougainville Cocoa Regulations. The gazettal and operationalisation of the BCRA legislation is significant as it allows the ABG to autonomously regulate its own agricultural commodity sector, and in turn increase farmer income and government revenue. As a result of the change, in 2023 for the first time, the PNG Cocoa Board provided DPI 70% of the export levies collected from Bougainville cocoa to the ABG. In 2024, ABG will be able to collect 100% of revenue from export levies directly.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
